  "comparison_rules": [
    "Native MPSC/CBF and neural-CBF filters must be compared only on tasks/configurations where their constraints and action semantics match.",
    "Modern conformal SLS-MPC and GPU-SLS references count as headline comparators only after pinned reproduction or documented mathematical adaptation.",
    "Hardware-accelerated runtime comparisons must publish hardware, solver, precision, deadline and compute budgets; do not infer speed superiority from different hardware.",
    "A-SLS (2026-10-14 preprint) is a priority comparator for active learning because it plans with guaranteed future parameter-uncertainty reduction; do not describe interval-gap active probing as equivalent to A-SLS.",
    "A geometric pairwise-separation probe may claim guaranteed one-step distinguishability only when all candidate observation sets are disjoint after declared measurement-noise expansion.",
    "Report matched episode-pair effect estimates with uncertainty; use exact one-sided binomial upper confidence limits for episode violation rates.",
    "Analyze each scenario and shielded setting separately before any predeclared cross-task aggregation; do not claim universal superiority from one pairwise p-value.",
    "The paired-inference CLI synthetic self-test artifact is qualification evidence for the analysis tool only, not external control-performance evidence.",
    "Never pool raw return, violation cost, latency, or other quantities with incompatible units; normalize each performance score using fixed task-specific anchors before task-stratified aggregation.",
    "Report task rows and equal-task-weight macro summaries together; task-level safety rates and exact upper limits remain separately visible.",
    "The stratified bootstrap resamples matched episode pairs within each task and treats the selected task suite as fixed; it does not establish generalization to unseen tasks.",
    "The stratified CLI's paired win rate is a within-seed outcome comparison with half credit for ties and is not RLiable's independent-sample probability-of-improvement estimator."
  ],
